@using Fhi.Munin.Explorer.Blazor
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Kildeutforskeren i helsedatas stiler";
}

@* The kildeutforsker under the same chrome and the same stylesheet as the front page, and it is
   here for one measurement the front page cannot make: the kilder table is the widest thing this
   package draws, and what it overflows is the HOST's page rather than its own box.

   Nothing else in either sample host could see that. Both style the component themselves on a
   page with room to spare; only here does the component get helsedata's real result column —
   1488px of page container minus 48px of air, minus a 384px filter sidebar and its gutter — and
   only at a narrow viewport does that column go under the table's min-content width
   (Fhi.Metadata-b3brc).

   `container` is what helsedata's own MuninUtforsker.cshtml wraps the mount in, copied for the
   reason the front page copies it: their Munin page has nothing above the component either.

   `KildeExplorer`, not `KildeSearch`, because that is the mount a legacy MVC host is meant to
   use — it is the one that reads the query string and writes back to the address. *@
<div class="container">
    <component type="typeof(KildeExplorer)"
               render-mode="Server"
               param-Language="@("no")"
               param-VariableExplorerPath="@("/")" />
</div>
